    "dea1992_electorate": "Electorate of the district electoral area at the 1991 register as given in the District Electoral Areas Commissioner's final report, 1992"
  },
  "citation": "Recommendations for the Grouping of Wards into District Electoral Areas for the purpose of Local Government Elections in Northern Ireland: Report by the District Electoral Areas Commissioner, Dr Maurice Hayes (Belfast: HMSO, December 1992), Appendix I. The same figures are printed as \"Area Electorate\" on OSNI, Local Government District Electoral Areas: 1992, Maps 1-4, Final Recommendations (Crown copyright 1992), from which they were read.",
  "checks": "The 101 figures sum to 1,132,617. Every district sums to the district electorate printed on the final maps (Antrim 29,937; Ards 48,467; Armagh 35,997; Ballymena 41,841; Ballymoney 17,457; Banbridge 26,402; Belfast 210,712; Carrickfergus 23,969; Castlereagh 47,350; Coleraine 36,756; Cookstown 21,479; Craigavon 53,873; Derry 62,326; Down 39,905; Dungannon 32,054; Fermanagh 38,601; Larne 22,107; Limavady 18,983; Lisburn 68,451; Magherafelt 25,288; Moyle 10,439; Newry and Mourne 55,974; Newtownabbey 54,624; North Down 53,780; Omagh 30,611; Strabane 25,234) and to the provisional (Aug 1992) district total. The 90 areas unchanged from the provisional stage agree with its Appendix I. The Carrickfergus areas also agree with the ward electors on OSNI sheet ADMINLGD92CARSH1 (Final Recommendations for District and Wards: 1992). For Cookstown and Dungannon the scan crop showed the area figures only in part (Torrent 9,082 in full; the trailing digits of the others), all agreeing with the provisional figures, which are used; the printed district totals confirm them.",
  "status": "Applied 2026-10-31 to render/source-cache/vector-intake/deas-1993.fgb and the deas-1993-vector-test tiles; FGB and PMTiles not yet uploaded to R2.",
